# Every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable is inlined into the JS bundle as a plain string
# literal at build time, and `strings` on the shipped Hermes bytecode recovers
# it. So this file holds configuration, never a secret — the client has no
# mechanism for one. Dropping the prefix does not buy secrecy either: the value
# is then not inlined at all and reads as `undefined` on a device.
#
# A release takes this value from its build profile, not from a local .env.
# A dev value baked into a release aborts at boot, by design: src/config/env.ts
# refuses cleartext http outside __DEV__.

# Base URL of the api-clean-platform instance this app talks to.
# The API defaults to port 3000.
#
# iOS simulator / web:  http://localhost:3000
# Android emulator:     http://10.0.2.2:3000   (localhost is the emulator itself)
# Physical device:      http://<your-machine-lan-ip>:3000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
